Since we load a prelude which is an important part of the
implementation, but is also distributed as source-form and could be
modified, independently, let the prelude file define its own version:

bocl:*prelude-version*

and if it's different than bocl binary version, then
lisp-implementation-version returns a concatenation:
(format nil "~A-~A" bocl:*version* bocl:*prelude-version*)



The results of these functions:

- short-site-name
- long-site-name
- machine-instance

may be overriden by the user by setting these variables:

- bocl:*short-site-name*
- bocl:*long-site-name*
- bocl:*machine-instance*

If they're nil or unbound, then the implementation will try to obtain them from the OS. (hostname)



Concerning the -LIMIT and MOST- and LEAST- variable values, they may
depend on the target platform (eg. 32-bit vs. 64-bit), so they cannot
just be hardwired in the code, each compiled executable/library must
return the correct values for its platform.

All these results must be documented in a complete platform table.


======================================================================
RESOLVED (v1.1.1)
======================================================================

All the platform functions return live run-time values:
  (lisp-implementation-type)    => "BOCL"
  (lisp-implementation-version) => "1.1.1"
  (machine-type)/(machine-version)/(machine-instance) => uname.machine / .version / gethostname
  (software-type)/(software-version)                  => uname.sysname / .release
  (short-site-name) => short host name ; (long-site-name) => FQDN (getaddrinfo
    AI_CANONNAME, falling back to the host name when it cannot be resolved).

SHORT-SITE-NAME and LONG-SITE-NAME are now kernel built-ins (sources/bocl.c,
mapping the site name to the host identity per the table above); the prelude
NIL stubs were removed so they are not shadowed.

The -LIMIT / MOST- / LEAST- variables are all defined. The previously-missing
ones were added in bootstrap/prelude.lisp: every long-float and the normalized
short-float MOST-/LEAST- limits (bocl has one float type, so they map to
double-float), and all eight {double,single,short,long}-float[-negative]-epsilon
constants (DBL_EPSILON). Verified bound at run time.
